Error [jet.TypestateMarkerRetired]: `#State` markers on `Lamp` are retired
  --> tests/ui/typestate/state_marker_is_retired.jet:5:5
    |
  5 |     #State(_ -> Off) make: fn(watts: Int) -> Lamp { Lamp{watts: watts} }
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: State types carry these facts: a parameter typed `Owner.A` requires `A`, a result typed `Owner.B` moves the value to `B`, and the owner's state list names each move as `A -> B`
 Fix: Run `jet fix` to write each marker's states into its signature and its moves into the state list of `Lamp`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0175
